message.content:
I'll build a playable piano with Web Audio synthesis — no samples needed, so every note is generated locally with correct equal-temperament frequencies. For the recording feature, I'll capture note events (not audio), which lets me offer playback with a visual "ghost player" showing which keys are being hit.

**Design direction:** I want this to feel like a real instrument, not a web widget. Dark stage-like backdrop, a warm wooden cabinet framing the keys, keys with real depth and press animation. A serif display face (Fraunces) for character, and a small event log strip that types out note names as you play — the page should feel alive while you play.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>Parlor — A Small Piano</title>
<link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Fraunces:opsz,wght@9..144,400;9..144,600;9..144,700&family=IBM+Plex+Mono:wght@400;500&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
<style>
  :root {
    --bg: #14100d;
    --cabinet: #2a1f16;
    --cabinet-hi: #3a2c1e;
    --felt: #7a2e2a;
    --wood: #b98a52;
    --cream: #f2ead8;
    --ink: #1a1512;
    --amber: #e8a33d;
  }
  * { margin: 0; padding: 0; box-sizing: border-box; }
  html, body { height: 100%; }
  body {
    background: var(--bg);
    background-image: radial-gradient(ellipse 80% 60% at 50% 0%, #241b13 0%, var(--bg) 70%);
    color: var(--cream);
    font-family: 'Fraunces', serif;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    min-height: 100vh;
    overflow-x: hidden;
    user-select: none;
    -webkit-user-select: none;
  }

  header { text-align: center; margin-top: 34px; }
  header h1 {
    font-size: clamp(28px, 4vw, 44px);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
    color: var(--cream);
  }
  header h1 em { font-style: italic; color: var(--wood); }
  header p {
    font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace;
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.22em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: #8a7a63;
    margin-top: 8px;
  }

  /* ---------- Transport ---------- */
  .transport {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 10px;
    margin: 26px 0 18px;
    padding: 10px 14px;
    background: #1d1712;
    border: 1px solid #33281d;
    border-radius: 10px;
  }
  .tbtn {
    font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace;
    font-size: 12px;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    padding: 9px 16px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    border: 1px solid #3d3122;
    background: #262019;
    color: var(--cream);
    cursor: pointer;
    transition: background .15s, border-color .15s, color .15s, transform .05s;
  }
  .tbtn:hover:not(:disabled) { background: #322a20; border-color: #55452e; }
  .tbtn:active:not(:disabled) { transform: translateY(1px); }
  .tbtn:disabled { opacity: .35; cursor: not-allowed; }
  .tbtn.recording {
    background: #4a1d18; border-color: #8a3a30; color: #ffb4a8;
    animation: pulse 1.1s ease-in-out infinite;
  }
  @keyframes pulse { 50% { box-shadow: 0 0 0 4px rgba(180, 60, 45, .18); } }
  .tbtn .dot {
    display: inline-block; width: 8px; height: 8px; border-radius: 50%;
    background: #e05545; margin-right: 7px; vertical-align: 1px;
  }
  .tbtn.recording .dot { animation: blink 1s steps(2) infinite; }
  @keyframes blink { 50% { opacity: .25; } }

  .clock {
    font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace;
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--amber);
    min-width: 64px;
    text-align: center;
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }
  .transport .sep { width: 1px; height: 22px; background: #33281d; }

  /* ---------- Piano ---------- */
  .piano-shell {
    background: linear-gradient(180deg, var(--cabinet-hi), var(--cabinet) 30%);
    border: 1px solid #4a3a26;
    border-radius: 14px 14px 8px 8px;
    padding: 14px 16px 0;
    box-shadow: 0 30px 60px -20px rgba(0,0,0,.7), inset 0 1px 0 rgba(255,255,255,.06);
    max-width: 920px;
    width: calc(100% - 32px);
  }
  .nameboard {
    display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: baseline;
    padding: 2px 6px 12px;
  }
  .nameboard .brand {
    font-size: 15px; font-weight: 600; font-style: italic; color: var(--wood);
    letter-spacing: .04em;
  }
  .nameboard .model {
    font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace; font-size: 10px;
    letter-spacing: .2em; color: #6b5a44; text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .felt-line { height: 7px; background: var(--felt); border-radius: 3px 3px 0 0;
    box-shadow: inset 0 -3px 5px rgba(0,0,0,.35); }

  .keyboard {
    position: relative;
    display: flex;
    height: 210px;
    background: #0c0a08;
    padding: 0 2px 2px;
    border-radius: 0 0 8px 8px;
    touch-action: none;
  }
  .key {
    position: relative;
    border-radius: 0 0 5px 5px;
    cursor: pointer;
  }
  .key.white {
    flex: 1;
    background: linear-gradient(180deg, #fbf6ea 0%, #efe7d4 82%, #d9cfb8 100%);
    border: 1px solid #b8ad94;
    border-top: none;
    margin-right: 1px;
    box-shadow: inset 0 -6px 8px -4px rgba(0,0,0,.18), 0 3px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.4);
    transform-origin: top;
    transition: transform .04s, box-shadow .04s, background .1s;
  }
  .key.white.down {
    transform: translateY(2px) rotateX(1.5deg);
    background: linear-gradient(180deg, #e9dfc8 0%, #ddd2b6 100%);
    box-shadow: inset 0 -2px 5px -2px rgba(0,0,0,.3), 0 1px 1px rgba(0,0,0,.4);
  }
  .key.white .label {
    position: absolute; bottom: 8px; left: 50%; transform: translateX(-50%);
    font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace; font-size: 10px; color: #a2957a;
  }
  .key.black {
    position: absolute;
    top: 0;
    width: calc(100% / 21 * 0.62);
    height: 62%;
    background: linear-gradient(180deg, #2e2a26 0%, #171412 70%, #000 100%);
    border: 1px solid #000;
    border-radius: 0 0 4px 4px;
    box-shadow: 0 4px 5px rgba(0,0,0,.6), inset 0 -3px 4px rgba(255,255,255,.06);
    z-index: 2;
    transition: transform .04s, box-shadow .04s;
  }
  .key.black.down {
    transform: translateY(2px);
    box-shadow: 0 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.6), inset 0 -1px 3px rgba(255,255,255,.04);
  }
  .key .ghost {
    position: absolute; inset: 0; border-radius: inherit; pointer-events: none;
    opacity: 0; transition: opacity .12s;
  }
  .key.white .ghost { background: linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(232,163,61,.0), rgba(232,163,61,.45)); }
  .key.black .ghost { background: linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(232,163,61,.15), rgba(232,163,61,.6)); }
  .key.ghosted .ghost { opacity: 1; }

  /* ---------- Log strip ---------- */
  .log-strip {
    width: calc(100% - 32px); max-width: 920px;
    margin: 18px 0 30px;
    height: 44px;
    display: flex; align-items: center;
    padding: 0 16px;
    background: #1d1712;
    border: 1px solid #33281d;
    border-radius: 8px;
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .log-strip .tag {
    font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace; font-size: 10px; letter-spacing: .18em;
    color: #6b5a44; text-transform: uppercase; margin-right: 14px; flex-shrink: 0;
  }
  #log {
    font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace; font-size: 12px; color: #c9b892;
    white-space: nowrap; overflow: hidden;
    mask-image: linear-gradient(90deg, transparent, #000 6%, #000 94%, transparent);
  }
  #log .n { margin-right: 14px; }
  #log .n b { color: var(--amber); font-weight: 500; }
  #log .n span { color: #7d6f58; }

  footer {
    font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace; font-size: 10px; letter-spacing: .14em;
    color: #5c5040; text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 26px; text-align: center;
    padding: 0 20px;
  }
  footer kbd {
    border: 1px solid #3d3122; border-radius: 4px; padding: 1px 5px;
    background: #262019; color: #a2957a; font-family: inherit;
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<header>
  <h1>The <em>Parlor</em> Piano</h1>
  <p>Twenty-one keys · tuned to A440</p>
</header>

<div class="transport">
  <button class="tbtn" id="recBtn"><span class="dot"></span>Record</button>
  <button class="tbtn" id="playBtn" disabled>Play</button>
  <button class="tbtn" id="stopBtn" disabled>Stop</button>
  <div class="sep"></div>
  <div class="clock" id="clock">0:00.0</div>
</div>

<div class="piano-shell">
  <div class="nameboard">
    <span class="brand">Parlor &amp; Sons</span>
    <span class="model">No. 21 · Upright</span>
  </div>
  <div class="felt-line"></div>
  <div class="keyboard" id="keyboard"></div>
</div>

<div class="log-strip">
  <span class="tag">Now playing</span>
  <div id="log"></div>
</div>

<footer>Play with your keyboard: <kbd>A</kbd>–<kbd>K</kbd> white keys · <kbd>W</kbd><kbd>E</kbd> <kbd>T</kbd><kbd>Y</kbd><kbd>U</kbd> black keys · Z / X shift octave</footer>

<script>
(() => {
  'use strict';

  /* ================= Audio engine ================= */
  let ctx = null;
  const master = { gain: null };
  function ensureAudio() {
    if (!ctx) {
      ctx = new (window.AudioContext || window.webkitAudioContext)();
      master.gain = ctx.createGain();
      master.gain.gain.value = 0.5;
      // gentle warmth
      const comp = ctx.createDynamicsCompressor();
      master.gain.connect(comp).connect(ctx.destination);
    }
    if (ctx.state === 'suspended') ctx.resume();
  }

  // Equal temperament: f = 440 * 2^((midi-69)/12)
  const freqOf = midi => 440 * Math.pow(2, (midi - 69) / 12);

  const NAMES = ['C','C#','D','D#','E','F','F#','G','G#','A','A#','B'];
  const nameOf = midi => NAMES[midi % 12] + (Math.floor(midi / 12) - 1);

  function playNote(midi, vel = 1) {
    ensureAudio();
    const t = ctx.currentTime;
    const f = freqOf(midi);
    const out = ctx.createGain();
    out.connect(master.gain);

    // Piano-ish tone: fundamental + a few harmonics with independent decay
    const partials = [
      { m: 1,    g: 1.0,  d: 1.0 },
      { m: 2,    g: 0.42, d: 0.72 },
      { m: 3,    g: 0.20, d: 0.55 },
      { m: 4.01, g: 0.10, d: 0.42 },  // slightly inharmonic
      { m: 5.02, g: 0.05, d: 0.30 },
    ];
    const dur = 2.6 + (108 - midi) * 0.012; // bass rings longer
    partials.forEach(p => {
      const o = ctx.createOscillator();
      o.type = 'sine';
      o.frequency.value = f * p.m;
      const g = ctx.createGain();
      const peak = p.g * vel * 0.32;
      g.gain.setValueAtTime(0, t);
      g.gain.linearRampToValueAtTime(peak, t + 0.006);
      g.gain.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(0.0001, t + dur * p.d);
      o.connect(g).connect(out);
      o.start(t);
      o.stop(t + dur * p.d + 0.1);
    });

    // Hammer thump: filtered noise burst
    const nb = ctx.createBuffer(1, ctx.sampleRate * 0.05, ctx.sampleRate);
    const nd = nb.getChannelData(0);
    for (let i = 0; i < nd.length; i++) nd[i] = (Math.random() * 2 - 1) * (1 - i / nd.length);
    const ns = ctx.createBufferSource();
    ns.buffer = nb;
    const nf = ctx.createBiquadFilter();
    nf.type = 'bandpass'; nf.frequency.value = f * 2.2; nf.Q.value = 0.8;
    const ng = ctx.createGain();
    ng.gain.setValueAtTime(0.18 * vel, t);
    ng.gain.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(0.0001, t + 0.05);
    ns.connect(nf).connect(ng).connect(out);
    ns.start(t);
  }

  /* ================= Keyboard build ================= */
  // C3 .. B4 = 21 keys (midi 48..68)
  const LOW = 48, HIGH = 68;
  const BLACK = [1, 3, 6, 8, 10];
  const keyboard = document.getElementById('keyboard');
  const keyEls = new Map();
  const whiteOrder = [];

  for (let m = LOW; m <= HIGH; m++) {
    if (!BLACK.includes(m % 12)) whiteOrder.push(m);
  }
  // white keys first (flex), black keys absolutely positioned
  whiteOrder.forEach(m => {
    const el = document.createElement('div');
    el.className = 'key white';
    el.dataset.midi = m;
    if ([0, 4].includes(m % 12)) {
      const l = document.createElement('span');
      l.className = 'label';
      l.textContent = nameOf(m);
      el.appendChild(l);
    }
    el.appendChild(Object.assign(document.createElement('div'), { className: 'ghost' }));
    keyboard.appendChild(el);
    keyEls.set(m, el);
  });
  whiteOrder.forEach((m, i) => {
    if (BLACK.includes((m + 1) % 12) && m + 1 <= HIGH) {
      const el = document.createElement('div');
      el.className = 'key black';
      el.dataset.midi = m + 1;
      const w = 100 / whiteOrder.length;
      el.style.left = `calc(${(i + 1) * w}% - ${(w * 0.62) / 2}% + 2px)`;
      el.appendChild(Object.assign(document.createElement('div'), { className: 'ghost' }));
      keyboard.appendChild(el);
      keyEls.set(m + 1, el);
    }
  });

  /* ================= Log strip ================= */
  const log = document.getElementById('log');
  function logNote(midi) {
    const s = document.createElement('span');
    s.className = 'n';
    s.innerHTML = `<b>${nameOf(midi)}</b><span> ·</span>`;
    log.appendChild(s);
    while (log.children.length > 40) log.removeChild(log.firstChild);
    log.scrollLeft = log.scrollWidth;
  }

  /* ================= Note on/off ================= */
  const active = new Map(); // midi -> {el, timer}
  function noteOn(midi, vel = 1, fromPlayback = false) {
    if (active.has(midi)) return;
    playNote(midi, vel);
    logNote(midi);
    const el = keyEls.get(midi);
    if (el) {
      el.classList.add('down');
      if (fromPlayback) el.classList.add('ghosted');
      active.set(midi, { el, fromPlayback });
    } else {
      active.set(midi, { el: null, fromPlayback });
    }
  }
  function noteOff(midi) {
    const a = active.get(midi);
    if (!a) return;
    if (a.el) {
      a.el.classList.remove('down');
      if (a.fromPlayback) {
        setTimeout(() => a.el.classList.remove('ghosted'), 150);
      }
    }
    active.delete(midi);
  }

  /* Pointer input — supports glissando across keys */
  let pointerDown = false;
  let lastPointerMidi = null;
  keyboard.addEventListener('pointerdown', e => {
    const el = e.target.closest('.key');
    if (!el) return;
    ensureAudio();
    pointerDown = true;
    keyboard.setPointerCapture(e.pointerId);
    const m = +el.dataset.midi;
    lastPointerMidi = m;
    noteOn(m);
  });
  keyboard.addEventListener('pointermove', e => {
    if (!pointerDown) return;
    const el = document.elementFromPoint(e.clientX, e.clientY)?.closest('.key');
    if (!el) return;
    const m = +el.dataset.midi;
    if (m !== lastPointerMidi) {
      if (lastPointerMidi !== null) noteOff(lastPointerMidi);
      lastPointerMidi = m;
      noteOn(m);
    }
  });
  const endPointer = () => {
    if (lastPointerMidi !== null) noteOff(lastPointerMidi);
    pointerDown = false;
    lastPointerMidi = null;
  };
  keyboard.addEventListener('pointerup', endPointer);
  keyboard.addEventListener('pointercancel', endPointer);

  /* ================= Computer keyboard ================= */
  const KEYMAP = { a:0, w:1, s:2, e:3, d:4, f:5, t:6, g:7, y:8, h:9, u:10, j:11, k:12, o:13, l:14, p:15 };
  let octaveShift = 0;
  const heldKeys = new Set();
  document.addEventListener('keydown', e => {
    if (e.repeat) return;
    const k = e.key.toLowerCase();
    if (k === 'z') { octaveShift = Math.max(-2, octaveShift - 1); return; }
    if (k === 'x') { octaveShift = Math.min(1, octaveShift + 1); return; }
    if (k === ' ') { e.preventDefault(); return; }
    if (!(k in KEYMAP) || heldKeys.has(k)) return;
    const m = LOW + octaveShift * 12 + KEYMAP[k];
    if (m < LOW || m > HIGH) return;
    heldKeys.add(k);
    ensureAudio();
    noteOn(m);
  });
  document.addEventListener('keyup', e => {
    const k = e.key.toLowerCase();
    if (!heldKeys.has(k)) return;
    heldKeys.delete(k);
    noteOff(LOW + octaveShift * 12 + KEYMAP[k]);
  });

  /* ================= Recorder ================= */
  const recBtn = document.getElementById('recBtn');
  const playBtn = document.getElementById('playBtn');
  const stopBtn = document.getElementById('stopBtn');
  const clock = document.getElementById('clock');

  let recording = false, playing = false;
  let recStart = 0, events = [], playTimers = [];
  let clockRAF = 0;

  function fmt(ms) {
    const s = ms / 1000;
    return `${Math.floor(s / 60)}:${String(Math.floor(s % 60)).padStart(2, '0')}.${Math.floor((s % 1) * 10)}`;
  }
  function tickClock(base) {
    cancelAnimationFrame(clockRAF);
    const loop = () => { clock.textContent = fmt(performance.now() - base); clockRAF = requestAnimationFrame(loop); };
    clockRAF = requestAnimationFrame(loop);
  }

  recBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
    if (playing) stopPlayback();
    recording = true;
    events = [];
    recStart = performance.now();
    recBtn.classList.add('recording');
    recBtn.innerHTML = '<span class="dot"></span>Recording';
    playBtn.disabled = true;
    stopBtn.disabled = false;
    tickClock(recStart);
  });

  function stopRecording() {
    recording = false;
    recBtn.classList.remove('recording');
    recBtn.innerHTML = '<span class="dot"></span>Record';
    stopBtn.disabled = true;
    playBtn.disabled = events.length === 0;
    cancelAnimationFrame(clockRAF);
    clock.textContent = fmt(events.length ? events[events.length - 1].t : 0);
  }

  function stopPlayback() {
    playing = false;
    playTimers.forEach(clearTimeout);
    playTimers = [];
    active.forEach((_, m) => noteOff(m));
    stopBtn.disabled = true;
    playBtn.disabled = events.length === 0;
    cancelAnimationFrame(clockRAF);
    clock.textContent = '0:00.0';
  }

  playBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
    if (recording) stopRecording();
    if (!events.length) return;
    ensureAudio();
    playing = true;
    playBtn.disabled = true;
    recBtn.disabled = true;
    stopBtn.disabled = false;
    const base = performance.now();
    tickClock(base);
    events.forEach(ev => {
      playTimers.push(setTimeout(() => {
        if (!playing) return;
        if (ev.type === 'on') noteOn(ev.midi, ev.vel, true);
        else noteOff(ev.midi);
      }, ev.t));
    });
    const total = events[events.length - 1].t + 800;
    playTimers.push(setTimeout(() => { if (playing) stopPlayback(); }, total));
  });

  stopBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
    if (recording) stopRecording();
    else if (playing) stopPlayback();
  });

  // Hook note events into the recorder
  const _on = noteOn, _off = noteOff;
  noteOn = function(midi, vel = 1, fromPlayback = false) {
    if (recording && !fromPlayback) events.push({ type: 'on', midi, vel, t: performance.now() - recStart });
    _on(midi, vel, fromPlayback);
  };
  noteOff = function(midi) {
    if (recording) events.push({ type: 'off', midi, t: performance.now() - recStart });
    _off(midi);
  };
})();
</script>
</body>
</html>
```

**How it works:**

- **Sound** — Each note is synthesized live: five sine partials (with slight inharmonicity on the upper ones, like real strings) plus a short band-passed noise burst for the hammer strike. Frequencies use exact equal temperament: `440 × 2^((midi−69)/12)`. Bass notes ring longer than treble, and a compressor keeps chords from clipping.

- **Recording** — I record *events* (note-on/off with timestamps and velocity), not audio. This keeps the file tiny and enables the **ghost playback**: during playback, the keys physically press down and glow amber as if a ghost pianist is playing your take. The transport bar has Record / Play / Stop with a live tenth-of-a-second clock.

- **Playing** — Mouse/touch with glissando (drag across keys), plus computer keyboard mapping (A–K row for whites, W/E/T/Y/U for blacks, Z/X to shift octave). A "Now playing" strip types out note names as you perform.

- **Design** — A dark stage with a warm wooden cabinet, felt-red strip above the keys, ivory keys with real press depth, and Fraunces serif for the "Parlor & Sons" nameboard — it should read as an instrument, not a UI.
